{
 "id": "2026-yuan-floral",
 "name": "Floral Display Booth Colours (Song Dynasty Style): Semantic Differential",
 "description": "Faithful replication of Yuan, Fan, Qin & Gong (2026), Buildings 16:181. Five virtual exhibition booths show the same two Song Dynasty-style floral arrangements and a classical text (Hua Jiu Xi); only the dominant background colour and the accent text colour differ, taken from Song Dynasty paintings: S1 sky blue + medium green (natural environment), S2 vermilion + blue and S3 vermilion + green (imperial palace), S4 earth red + white and S5 earth red + light yellow (scholar's studio). As in the paper, each booth is shown full screen for 15 s in random order with 5 s of black screen between images; then each booth is shown again and rated on four 5-point semantic differential indicators: traditional cultural atmosphere (Song Dynasty traditional – contemporary avant-garde), colour matching comfort, artwork form clarity and explanatory text clarity. Gender, age, education and background in colour cognition or floral arrangement are asked at the end. Stimuli: the paper's own booth images (Figure 3b; floral works photographed at the 2019 Beijing International Horticultural Exhibition), cropped from the CC BY 4.0 article; credited on the page and removed if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) the paper recorded eye movements with Tobii Pro Glasses 2 on a colour-calibrated 24-inch monitor in a dark room; this template records only presentation order and time, and screen colour is not controlled; (2) the images come from the published figure (about 615 × 430 px), so the small classical text is less legible than in the original 1920 × 1080 display, which affects the text clarity rating; (3) the order of the rating pages is randomised, which the paper does not describe.",
